<ContentLayout title="About TokenCalculator.dev" description="Technical methodology behind the privacy-first, browser-based TokenCalculator.dev engine." heading="About"><p><strong>TokenCalculator.dev</strong> is an independent, privacy-first browser-based utility for developers, prompt engineers, and teams analyzing prompt size, API input cost, and context-window utilization before calling an LLM.</p><h2>Mission</h2><p>The calculator is maintained around three commitments: text, document contents, and image pixels remain on-device; calculation provenance is exposed for every result; and changing model facts link back to public sources.</p><h2>Tokenizer methodology</h2><p>OpenAI-family text uses <a href="https://github.com/dqbd/tiktoken">js-tiktoken</a> with the model’s configured BPE encoding and vocabulary. Where an equivalent offline production tokenizer is not distributed, Claude, Gemini, and DeepSeek use a deterministic <strong>Provider-Calibrated UTF-8 Token Projection</strong>: UTF-8 byte length is normalized by a provider-family bytes-per-token coefficient. Every result identifies its computation path.</p><h2>Open model data</h2><p>Pricing and context-window limits are refreshed from the open-source <a href="https://models.dev/">Models.dev</a> catalog. A bundled, versioned registry keeps the calculator available when that public catalog cannot be reached. Provider invoices and official documentation remain authoritative.</p><h2>Editorial responsibility</h2><p>Pricing corrections, methodology questions, and reproducible calculation issues can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@tokencalculator.dev">hello@tokencalculator.dev</a>. Substantive changes are reviewed against provider documentation before publication.</p><p><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> August 22, 2026.</p></ContentLayout>
